text \<open>
Earlier versions of this file gave rules that could need to be normalized by @{method auto}
for the word size to be equal on both sides of the equation, and the rule @{thm word_plus_and_or_coroll2}
to be used by @{method simp} in order to be able to apply the rule @{thm ucast_eqD} below.
This caused some unintended behaviour: @{method auto} or @{method simp} would normalize the word equations
to 32-bit operations. This often made absolutely no difference, but sometimes weird rules like @{thm sxword_plus_1}
would be applied instead, resulting in a string of word size comments like:
\begin{verbatim}
  bytes 0-127: 0 = 0
